From 8c9ad0d19e94fa42b7c1c1dc2a807129dfbb6d0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:57:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: apu-expert-pool -- the UMA budget split (VRAM 75 % of
 free RAM, pool 10 %, the rest to the OS) and a loud advisory when -ncmoe is
 pointless

Maintainer policy (2026-11-09): on a UMA APU "VRAM" and RAM are one medium, so the two tiers
are sized from the same figure and must not add up to all of it.

* `MOE_UMA_VRAM_PCT` (default 75) -- the arena / slab ceiling as a share of MemAvailable.  This
  replaces the ad-hoc 60 % P2.1 shipped with, and applies to the slab cap as well, so the
  movable-boundary slab can never map the machine.
* `MOE_UMA_POOL_PCT` (default 10) -- the auto-mode ceiling on the pinned expert pool on a UMA
  box.  Implemented as the UMA-aware default of `MOE_HOST_POOL_RAM_PCT`, which becomes "-1 =
  auto" (the operator's explicit value still wins on any platform, as does
  MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_MIB for the arena).  Both are CEILINGS, not reservations: a tier only takes
  what its tables need (measured: pool 3814 MiB against a 10.2 GiB ceiling, so the ceiling did
  not bind).
* ~15 % stays with the OS, the page cache and the model mapping the pool fills from -- which is
  the point: the page cache is the pool's source, so a budget of 100 % would fight itself.
* The advisory: when the model's own bytes fit in the APU's usable device memory, the loader
  says so LOUDLY and still honours the request -- `-ncmoe`/`-lme` buys no capacity there and
  gives away decode bandwidth, so `-ncmoe 0` is almost certainly faster.

Measured on halo (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, `-ncmoe 8 -lm mmap --host-experts pool`): the
advisory fires ("this model (21603.0 MiB) FITS in this APU's usable device memory
(89153.2 MiB = 75% of MemAvailable)"), the arena budget is 76 643 MiB (75 % of MemAvailable),
and greedy text stays byte-identical to `-ncmoe 0`.  `MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_UMA=0` disarms the slab.

Open: the >RAM acceptance arm is still unrun (it is the case the 75/10 split exists for, and
the one that would show the pool ceiling binding); the two INFO/WARN lines in the UMA preflight
arm still do not reach the log although the branch provably runs (census is authoritative).
